y very  strict  ruling on abortion and it would get  appealed all the way up to the supreme  court and the supreme court might say  this is okay if that were to happen  you have effectively by precedent undone  roe v  wade and you would have many things  change in red states  and not very much would change in uh  blue states the reality is  that if roe v wade were effectively  overturned by by creating new precedent  states like massachusetts other blue  states  are not likely to see any real changes  to the availability and access to safe  abortions the red states will get  absolutely crushed and this is another  one of those ways in which i've said  before even during the trump presidency  in blue states we are insulated  in many ways from the destructive effect  of a radical  ideological reactionary presidency like  that of donald trump  so as is often the case the destruction  brought forward by republican policy and  right-wing ideology  will disproportionately hurt  right-wingers when you look at  trump trying to undo obamacare  in massachusetts we already have  something that predates obamacare called  romneycare  and it is the folks in places like  mississippi which has one of the worst  one of the worst three  health care systems in the country it is  those folks  who are disproportionately hurt by  donald trump doing things like  undoing the individual mandate on  obamacare  so that's a reality that if they're able  to do it  not a lot will change in blue states a  lot will change in red states  now does the republican party really  want  roe v wade overturned the reason i ask  is if they actually  overturn it it's conceivable  that there will be number one  significantly renewed  enthusiasm against republicans at the  state level  in order to try to legalize abortion  in a lot of these states that are likely  to overturn it and  the reality is that since roe v wade was  was issued as a decision it has been a  great  fundraising tool for republicans  republicans raise a ton of money by  saying we've got to overturn roe v wade  we need you to vote for this person and  that person and that person from  low level positions all the way up to  the president  we need you to do it so we can get the  right people in power  to overturn roe v wade if they actually  do it  they no longer have that carrot to rile  up  evangelical voters i think that there is  some merit to that and i  question whether republicans really want  to overturn it or whether they want to  keep fighting about overturning it  because it allows them to raise money  it's a question but is roe v wade in  danger  with a six to three court particularly  if donald trump gets reelected  and particularly if we maintain a  republican senate yes  it is in danger what it will mean in  massachusetts is a different question
 

